From 228e900b90bb549e353958d17420497ca6248d81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] experiment: capture consumed target routes with scheduler
 coordinates

Record exact target IDs and route-weight hashes at the routed-expert call,
using the layer's actual SWA metadata key and explicit CED decoder tag.
Snapshot authoritative GPU query starts and join compact rows by request and
position after the target forward. Retain all verification rows before sampling,
including rows later rejected. Keep files private and bounded; no prompt or
input token content is saved. Refuse graph replay, DBO, PCP, batch sharding,
multiple anchors or an unrecognized row mapping rather than guessing.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Prepared-base: f3bfdf8b8c08870754cc3c756b75faa9156595e0
Rationale: accepted-token response traces omit actual rejected verification rows.
Quality: observational snapshots do not mutate routes or arithmetic; eager
capture and synchronization alter timing and possibly batching. Capture runs
cannot serve as performance evidence. Target-only; drafter capture excluded.
Tests: ten CPU mapping contracts, syntax checks, new-module ruff, diff check.
Native integration and model invariance remain pending.
Upstream-status: experiment-only instrumentation; no upstream proposal.
